# Source: docs/kegtron/UDPStreaming.pdf ("UDP Streaming", Kegtron, April 2026).
# Data Definitions section (page 3) defines the payload JSON shape used on every line
# below: num/fwRev/portCount/serialNum/temp at the top level, plus exactly one
# "port<i>" object per packet carrying abv/cleanActive/curServ/drinkSize/ibu/maker/
# lastServing/state/style/tapLabel/userDesc/userName/volDisp/volSize/volStart (curServ
# is UDP-only -- accumulated mL of the CURRENT serving; it clears to 0 once a serving
# ends and stays 0 until the next one starts).
# Behavior section (page 4) cadence modeled here: idle round-robin 1 packet/sec across
# ports (num 1-2), then 200ms samples while port0 pours (num 3-8, curServ rising
# 48->355), then curServ clears to 0 the instant flow stops while volDisp/lastServing
# jump to reflect the completed serving, continuing to stream at 200ms for the ~2s
# tail after flow stopped (num 9-10), then back to idle round-robin (num 11, port1).
# Group/port for production per page 5: multicast 239.50.50.50:50505 (this fixture
# carries only the payload; transport framing is exercised by the test itself).
# serialNum 2001011234 matches tests/fixtures/kegtron/device-shadow.json's serial, for
# cross-source continuity (Task 8 reconciles cloud <-> UDP by serial).
